# Generated by `python -m statuswall.cli` from live measurement. Regenerating it
# is one command, and committing it would put a timestamped snapshot of machine
# state into the design history, where it would read as a fact about the project
# rather than about one moment.
status-wall.html

# Written by the same pass, from the same probe results, and just as much a
# snapshot of one moment: phase rows counting tiles lit today.
build-progress.html

# Written by the same pass from the forward engine's fill journal: open
# positions and closed round trips as they stood at one instant. Added
# 2026-08-16 after it was committed by accident - this ignore list names files
# one by one, so every new generated board has to be added here, and the one
# that is forgotten is the one that gets committed. That is the cost of an
# ignore-list over an allowlist, and it is recorded rather than papered over.
blotter.html
